      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) such that the four-digit number \\( 712n \\) is divisible by 18, we need to use the rule that a number is divisible by 18 if and only if it is divisible by both 2 and 9. This means:\n1. The number must be even (i.e., \\( n \\) must be even).\n2. The number must be divisible by 9 (i.e., the sum of its digits must be divisible by 9).\n\nFirst, let's find the sum of the digits of \\( 712n \\):\n\\[ 7 + 1 + 2 + n = 10 + n. \\]\nFor \\( 712n \\) to be divisible by 9, \\( 10 + n \\) must be divisible by 9. The possible values for \\( 10 + n \\) that are divisible by 9 are 9, 18, 27, etc. Since \\( n \\) is a digit (0 through 9), the only possible value for \\( 10 + n \\) is 18. Therefore:\n\\[ 10 + n = 18 \\implies n = 18 - 10 \\implies n = 8. \\]\n\nWe should also check that \\( 7128 \\) is even. Since \\( 8 \\) is even, \\( 7128 \\) is divisible by 2, and thus by 18.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) that makes the number \\( 712n \\) divisible by 18 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
